---
title: 'Axis Position'
description: 'Control where each axis is rendered in an AG Charts cartesian chart and how axes cross with crossAt.'
---

Axes attach to the chart edges to provide scale and labels for series. Each cartesian axis can render on the `top`, `bottom`, `left`, or `right` edge depending on its orientation.

## Axis Placement

The axis `position` property controls where the axis is rendered. By default, horizontal axes appear at the bottom of the chart and vertical axes appear on the left.

```js format="snippet"
{
    axes: [
        {
            type: 'number',
            position: 'left',
        },
        {
            type: 'category',
            position: 'bottom',
        },
    ],
}
```

Axes with matching direction can share an edge. This allows, for example, a pair of y-axes on either side of the chart or two x-axes both on the top.

Secondary axes adopt their own configured `position`. If no position is supplied they default to the opposite side of the primary axis. See [Secondary Axes](./axes-secondary/) for more detail on pairing.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Axis Positions" name="axis-position-basic" type="generated" /%}

## CrossAt

The `crossAt` option allows an axis to intersect a perpendicular axis at a specific axis value instead of the default chart edge. This is useful for centring the chart origin or aligning axes to highlight particular thresholds.

```js format="snippet"
{
    axes: [
        {
            type: 'number',
            position: 'left',
            crossAt: { value: 0 },
        },
    ],
}
```

Specify `crossAt.value` to use a precise point from the opposing axis domain. When the target value leaves the visible range, by default the axis locks to the closest in range position. Set `sticky: false` to remove the axis when it is outside of the perpendicular axis' domain.

When using `crossAt`, ensure the target value falls within the axis domain so the axes can intersect within the visible chart area.

{% chartExampleRunner title="CrossAt" name="axis-cross-at" type="generated" /%}
